# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ASan/UBSan soak (ci/tools/soak.sh).
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NARROW
#
# nginx allocates its configuration out of the *cycle pool* and deliberately
# never frees it: the pool lives until the process exits, and tearing it down
# at shutdown would be pure work with no benefit. LeakSanitizer runs at exit
# and cannot know that, so it reports every config-time allocation still held
# by the cycle as leaked. The first soak run under LSan produced 137 blocks /
# ~136 KB, ALL of them rooted in ngx_init_cycle -- including allocations from
# stock modules this repo does not touch (ngx_http_fastcgi_create_loc_conf was
# the largest single block). Zero came from the request path.
#
# The blunt fix is ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0, which throws away the check
# entirely. Leak detection over the REQUEST path is a large part of why this
# soak exists -- a leak per request is exactly the bug class a 30s storm at
# concurrency 4 is meant to expose -- so instead the config-load roots are
# suppressed by frame and everything else keeps reporting.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: a genuine leak whose allocation happens during
# configuration parsing is invisible here. That is the accepted cost. A leak
# in a per-request or per-connection path -- the case that actually compounds
# under load -- is still caught, because it does not pass through these frames.
#
# MAINTENANCE
#   - Add a frame only after confirming the allocation is genuinely owned by
#     the cycle pool and lives until exit. "It is noisy" is not a reason.
#   - Never suppress a frame from the request path (ngx_http_*_handler,
#     ngx_http_autocert_serve_*, anything below ngx_http_process_request).
#   - Verify a change with:
#       ci/tools/soak.sh <asan-nginx> 30 4
#     and confirm the report is empty rather than merely smaller.

# nginx's own cycle/config initialisation. Everything the config parser
# allocates hangs off these, across all modules, built-in and dynamic.
leak:ngx_init_cycle
leak:ngx_conf_parse
leak:ngx_conf_handler

# The http{} block's per-module create/merge conf callbacks run under
# ngx_http_block, still on the cycle pool. This covers this module's
# ngx_http_autocert_postconfig / install_dummy config-time allocations and
# every stock module's alongside them.
leak:ngx_http_block

# OpenSSL objects created at config time and owned by the SSL context for the
# life of the cycle (SSL_CTX, its cert/key material, the dummy certificate
# installed before the first real issuance).
leak:ngx_ssl_create
leak:ngx_http_ssl_merge_srv_conf
leak:ngx_http_merge_servers
